# mjolnir/.env — ONLY values used by mjolnir and nothing else.
#
# Shared values live in the repository root `.env` (see /.env.example):
# TUN_SITE_ADDRESS, TUN_PUBLIC_BASE, OTA_TOKEN, OPERATOR_AUTH_TOKEN,
# MJOLNIR_POSTGRES_PASSWORD (renamed from POSTGRES_PASSWORD by D151 — one key
# per database, and backup/entrypoint.sh reads it by the new name),
# STABBUR_AUTH_TOKEN, BACKUP_*. Do not repeat any of them here — no value is
# defined in two files.
#
# Derived values are computed in compose.yaml and typed nowhere:
# DATABASE_URL, STABBUR_BASE_URL (http://stabbur-backend:5056),
# STABBUR_UI_BASE ($TUN_PUBLIC_BASE/stabbur/ui). The old *_UPSTREAM keys are
# gone entirely — caddy/Caddyfile names stabbur-backend, smia-backend and
# phonexa-backend directly, because one repository is one Compose project
# with one default network and a service name always resolves. There is no
# `tun-shared` network and no `docker network create` step.

# --- /phonexa gate (caddy/Caddyfile's basic_auth) ----------------------
# Optional: leave it unset and /phonexa/* FAILS CLOSED (401 on every
# request) — it is never served unauthenticated.
#
# Username is fixed to `operator`; the password is the root .env's
# OPERATOR_AUTH_TOKEN. basic_auth only accepts a hash and nothing derives
# one automatically, so make it once by hand:
#
#     docker run --rm caddy:2-alpine caddy hash-password \
#         --plaintext "<your OPERATOR_AUTH_TOKEN>"
#
# SINGLE-QUOTE the value: a bcrypt hash contains `$`, which compose
# interpolates away otherwise (double quotes do not help).
# ROTATION: changing OPERATOR_AUTH_TOKEN does NOT change this hash —
# regenerate it in the same deploy or the old password keeps working.
#
# Note phonexa shares this origin with hub and builder, whose session cookie
# is Path=/. HttpOnly stops phonexa-origin JS from reading it; it does not
# stop the browser sending it. Accepted when the operator chose a path over
# a subdomain.
# PHONEXA_AUTH_HASH='<caddy hash-password output, single-quoted>'

# --- hub / builder ------------------------------------------------------
# Source language for bundle/forecast work. Defaults to "no".
# SOURCE_LANG=no

# --- local/dev only — never set either on the VPS -----------------------
# ALLOW_HTTP=1
# ALLOW_NO_COMPANION=1
